An ElasticNet model was fitted using 10-fold cross-validation to jointly tune the mixing parameter α and the regularisation parameter λ. A grid of 10 α values ranging from 0 (Ridge) to 1 (LASSO) was evaluated alongside 100 λ values on a logarithmic scale from 10³ to 10⁻³. The optimal value of α was `r round(q3_best_alpha, 3)`, with λ_min = `r round(q3_lambda_min, 4)` and λ_1se = `r round(q3_lambda_1se, 4)`. The full cross-validation procedure completed in `r round(q3_time_elnet[3], 2)` seconds.


